{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>He chose the first portion for himself.</b> Gad saw and chose for himself the first part of the land of Israel, namely the land of Sihon and Og which is across the Jordan." "<b>For there the portion of the lawgiver is hidden.</b> As the Targum [renders]: therefore he took it for his portion, even though Ammon and Moab contest it — for he knew that the Holy One, blessed be He, was destined to bury Moses our Master there. And had it been destined to return to the hand of Ammon, the Holy One, blessed be He, would not have buried him there, outside the land." "<b>And he came at the heads of the people.</b> Gad went to war at the head of the people of Israel." "<b>He did the righteousness of YHWH.</b> He stood by his condition and its fulfillment, according to the stipulation he made with Israel to cross over before the vanguard."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:03.286501455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}